today we're breaking down halo  infinite's new maps and explaining why  kingdom hearts 4 sora looks so different  halo infinite season 2 lone wolves will  be here in just a few weeks and 343  industries has revealed the two new maps  spartans will be murdering each other on  named catalyst and breaker the maps are  very different from one another with one  focusing on cold industrial interiors  while the other is an open desert map  designed for big team battle for fans of  traditional arena style multiplayer you  can look forward to catalyst in a blog  post on halo waypoint multiplayer level  designer tyler entrue described it as a  tunnel-like map with 4runner structures  complete with the light bridge you've  come to know and love from halo it  shares some similarities with epitaph  from halo 3 and the ever popular haven  from halo 4 but with a scrappier feel  there is more banished influence as the  group relies heavily on captured  technology and weapons rather than its  own creations breaker is an open outdoor  map designed for big team battle  especially ctf matches with a base on  either side making for huge skirmishes  in the midsection huge pieces of wrecked  machinery are visible here building on  what you see throughout halo infinite's  campaign there's even a death pit that  you can jump in a warthog if you're  skilled enough but hitting the ramp  incorrectly will result in a very  unceremonious death halo infinite season  2 kicks off on may 3rd and also comes  with two new armor cores a new battle  pass and the modes land grab and king of  the hill and more story events switching  gears from chief to sora kingdom hearts  4 looks set to introduce a few graphical  changes to the long running series which  includes a more mature look for  protagonist sora and other updated  visual tweaks in a new interview with  famatsu that was translated by vgc  series creator tetsuya nomura spoke  about these changes and the world of  quadratum which serves as an afterlife  of sorts nomura said quote from sora's  perspective quadratum is an underworld a  fictional world that is different from  reality but from the point of view of  the inhabitants of the quadratum side  the world of quadratum is reality and  the world where sora and the others were  is the other side the fictional world  nomura added that goofy and donald duck  are searching for sora in kingdom hearts  4 and if he were to return to his  original reality he'd start to resemble  his more cartoonish design again as fans  have discovered quadratum has been  referenced before as an unreality  separate from the other realms in the  series with kingdom hearts 3 confirming  that location as part of a secret ending  kingdom hearts 4 is the start of a new  saga for sora and pals and while it'll  still be a while before the game  launches fans have begun scouring  footage for clues as to what they can  expect from the square enix and disney  collaboration some eagle eye fans claim  to have spotted a star wars tease in the  game's reveal trailer which isn't too  implausible given that disney owns the  sci-fi franchise but nomura isn't the  only series creator reacting to  something metal gear and death stranding  mastermind hideo kojima opened up about  sony acquisition rumors playstation  studios recently updated its first party  studios banner to include sam bridges  the protagonist of death stranding a  playstation console exclusive its  director's cup version was released on  both playstation consoles and pc kojima  posted the banner himself onto his  twitter account without providing any  further contacts fueling rumors that  sony may have acquired kojima  productions and that perhaps an official  announcement would be coming soon  however kojima retweeted his post and  apologized for the confusion he caused  he clarified quote i'm sorry for the  misunderstanding but kojima productions  has been and will continue to be an  independent studio kojima productions is  also working on a game with microsoft  amid these acquisition rumors kojima's  xbox project is reportedly still  progressing as planned let us know in  the comments if you're excited for  halo's new maps and we'll see you next  week  you
 

